WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.210
19 September 1819.

2
00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:06.030
Keats takes a Sunday walk near Winchester,

3
00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.510
and that day he writes a poem.

4
00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:09.710
Morning.

5
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:13.980
Mist over the field, and a
tree bending under its apples.

6
00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:18.670
"Season of mists and mellow
fruitfulness," Afternoon:

7
00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.540
corn half cut, a cider press.

8
00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.690
Evening: pink light on the stubble,
and swallows gathering in the sky.

9
00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:29.670
The day is ending, and so is the year.

10
00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:33.180
So why does Keats make
autumn feel so full?

11
00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:38.160
In this mission, you'll take apart the
crowded images of ripeness in stanza 1.

12
00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:40.640
You'll follow three
stanzas through a season,

13
00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:42.630
and through a single day.

14
00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:47.230
Your mission: explain why Keats
makes autumn feel so full.
